{"source_key":"sha256-767aea33d36d18c60bf3118db432de90","record_index":263,"record_hash":"sha256:25cb512f9ace673d71b4b65f052a50061f0a2636f4d6d1b8633bbfcf59d4e812","timestamp":"2026-07-23T14:42:05.813Z","kind":"message","source_event_kind":"codex:response_item:message","role":"assistant","text":"Recommended plan: reintroduce the prototype’s semantics, not its commits, and build directly on `d5ef042d4c`’s prepared-checkout API.\n\nThe detached-HEAD report is probably not caused by ref ordering. I reproduced:\n\n```text\ngit worktree add <path> origin/master\n## HEAD (no branch)\n```\n\nThat worktree is detached before GitButler touches it. The prototype used `skip_head_update: true`, so it could leave files/index stale but could not detach a symbolic HEAD.\n\n## Implementation plan\n\n1. Carry visible worktree identity into the graph.\n\n   - Add stable `name` to [`WorktreeTip`]([REDACTED:path]).\n   - Populate it from [`Context::graph_options()`]([REDACTED:path]).\n   - Continue using `active_worktrees()` as the sole feature-flag/archive boundary.\n   - Let `Editor::create()` consume `workspace.graph.options.worktree_tips`; avoid changing every Editor caller or introducing `Context::editor()`.\n\n2. Teach Editor about both HEAD shapes.\n\n   - Symbolic worktree: record a reference selector and make the visible local branch a mutable entrypoint.\n   - Detached worktree: record a commit selector, but do not make its entire segment mutable automatically—`origin/master` may share that segment.\n   - Add `Checkout::Worktree { name, selector, original_head_kind }` beside the current [`Checkout::Head`]([REDACTED:path]).\n   - Protect every branch checked out in a linked worktree from Editor deletion, even when archived or the flag is off. The minimal implementation is to exclude those refs from deletion candidates rather than carry another Editor-wide set.\n\n3. Keep preview graphs consistent.\n\n   - Recompute stored worktree tips from normalized checkout selectors during `overlayed_graph()`.\n   - This is essential for detached HEADs: they cannot be re-resolved through a branch ref.\n\n4. Replace the prototype’s materialization order.\n\n   Current materialization checks out before committing ref edits ([materialize.rs]([REDACTED:path])). Use:\n\n   1. Persist new objects.\n   2. Resolve and prepare the main plus every visible-worktree checkout against their old HEADs.\n   3. Abort without mutation if any worktree disappeared, switched HEAD shape, conflicts, or has overlapping dirt.\n   4. Apply all shared ref edits atomically.\n   5. Execute prepared linked checkouts, then the main checkout.\n   6. Refresh the workspace.\n\n   [`prepare_safe_checkout_from_head()`]([REDACTED:path]) already supports execution after symbolic refs move.\n\n   - Symbolic worktree: `skip_head_update = true`; its private HEAD remains byte-for-byte symbolic.\n   - Detached worktree: update its private HEAD to the mapped OID while keeping it detached.\n   - A checkout selector becoming `Step::None` should fail before mutation, not leave a stale worktree.\n   - `materialize_without_checkout()` should still update linked worktrees; “without checkout” should only exempt the Editor’s own worktree.\n\n5. Keep operation-specific pieces out for now.\n\n   Skip public preflight APIs, rollback journaling, and worktree-specific merge-base overrides until linked-worktree hunk consumption needs them. The remaining post-ref filesystem crash window is real, but adding distributed rollback across worktrees is not justified yet.\n\n## Acceptance tests\n\n- Flag off and archived worktrees receive no checkout behavior.\n- Symbolic worktree branch moves, unrelated dirt survives, index/files become clean, and raw HEAD stays `ref: refs/heads/...`.\n- A detached `origin/master` worktree starts detached and remains detached; if its selected commit is rewritten, its private HEAD advances without moving `origin/master`.\n- Two worktrees where the second conflicts: all refs, HEAD files, indexes, and files remain unchanged.\n- Checked-out refs cannot be deleted, independently of visibility.\n- `materialize_without_checkout()` leaves the main worktree alone while linked worktrees follow their HEADs.\n- One TUI-level reproduction of the reported commit flow.\n\nI’d deliver this as two focused commits: Editor identity/checkout modeling, then prepared materialization plus regressions. The current workspace is clean, and both foundation checks pass:\n\n- `prepared_checkouts_use_the_old_linked_worktree_heads_after_their_refs_move`\n- `workspace_from_head_seeds_active_worktree_tips`\n\n[GB-1753](https://linear.[REDACTED:entropy])\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:475-504|note=[prior linked worktree scope and TUI acceptance guidance]\nrollout_summaries/2026-07-15T19-48-26-92Kp-linked_worktree_tui_visibility_manipulation.md:19-31|note=[prototype integration breadth and TUI validation surface]\n<[REDACTED:path]>\n<rollout_ids>\n[REDACTED:entropy]\n<[REDACTED:path]>\n<[REDACTED:path]>","tool_name":null,"tool_input":null,"source_record":{"timestamp":"2026-07-23T14:42:05.813Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"[REDACTED:entropy]","role":"assistant","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"[REDACTED:entropy]"},"phase":"final_answer"}}}